From b98a7a54912cc8350162a9c65a47eff4a5b70607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:52:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: retrying, root-preferring lease on the host
 dispatcher/sync locks

A gateway that lost the boot-time flock on .dispatcher.lock or .sync.lock never retried, and
whichever gateway reached it first kept it for life. On hermes-hub a pinned profile gateway
(askeve-reviewer, old core, memory-derived max_in_progress=8 vs the root's 16) won every joint
restart and held both locks for hours while 64 cards sat ready.

- gateway/kanban_singleton.py: SingletonLease. Contended -> retry every 30s. The root gateway
  (HERMES_HOME == kanban root) posts <lock>.root-wanted when contended; a profile gateway waits a
  60s grace before its first attempt, never acquires while a live root claim exists, and yields a
  held lock when one appears (dispatcher: between ticks; sync: run_forever keep_running).
  Holder writes <lock>.holder.json; contention > 5 min logs a WARNING naming holder pid/HERMES_HOME.
- _check_dispatcher_presence asks who holds the host lock first, so a profile CLI with
  dispatch_in_gateway=false no longer warns 'task will sit in ready' while the root dispatches.
- kanban stats (text + JSON host_locks) names both lock holders and flags a non-root holder.
- describe_suppression/stuck warning add cap_source=<config path or memory-derived default>.
